                <head>About the Digital Edition</head>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations of the United States</hi>, 1981–1988,
                    Volume XVI, South America is part of a subseries of the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Foreign Relations</hi> series that documents the foreign policy decision
                    making of the administration of President Ronald Reagan. This web page explains
                    the current status of the volume’s digital edition.</p>
                <p>To provide timely access to the volume’s documents, the Office of the Historian
                    will publish chapters as they are cleared. To date, the following chapters have
                    been published:</p>
                <table>
                    <row role="label">
                        <cell><hi rendition="#bold">Title</hi></cell>
                        <cell><hi rendition="#bold">Publication Date</hi></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell><ref target="#ch7">Ecuador</ref></cell>
                        <cell>September 18, 2026</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell><ref target="#ch8">Paraguay</ref></cell>
                        <cell>September 18, 2026</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell><ref target="#ch10">Uruguay</ref></cell>
                        <cell>September 18, 2026</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell><ref target="#ch11">Venezuela</ref></cell>
                        <cell>September 18, 2026</cell>
                    </row>
                </table>
                <p>The volume’s <ref target="frus:frus1981-88v16">landing page</ref> provides a
                    complete list of its front matter and chapters, even those not yet published.
                    When readers access portions of the volume that have not yet been published,
                    they will encounter a note explaining this and linking to this page for further
                    details.</p>
                <p>Some front matter sections will be updated with each chapter. For example, <ref
                        target="#sources">Sources</ref> presents a list of the sources from the
                    chapters that have been published.</p>
                <p>The chapters and sections that have been published can be searched and viewed
                    online and downloaded as ebooks and as TEI XML.</p>
                <p>When the remainder of the volume is cleared for publication, a volume-length PDF
                    will be released.</p>
                <p>This page will be updated to note significant additions to the volume.</p>
                <p rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#bold">Last updated September 18,
                        2026</hi></p>
            </div>
